    "body": "### Discussed in https://github.com/encode/starlette/discussions/1778\r\n\r\n<div type='discussions-op-text'>\r\n\r\n<sup>Originally posted by **jvail** July 27, 2022</sup>\r\nHi,\r\n\r\nI may have missed the discussion/issue but I wonder what the reason might be to not support negative values in the default float & int convertors?\r\n\r\nI have now implemented them myself (by copying starlette's default converters and changing the regex). But of course I'd prefer not to do that.\r\n\r\nThank you\r\nJan</div>\r\n\r\nWould you accept a PR for this? I am using the regex from here https://docs.python.org/3/library/re.html#simulating-scanf. So fairly reliable, I guess.\r\n",
